KG42.register("rules-b5b0f55cd6e06a6c798edfdb",{"id":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R002","paper":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Demand submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The DMO combines received demand bids and submits an aggregated demand bid to the ISO. Scope: DMO aggregation of microgrid and other responsive-load demand bids for submission to the ISO. Microgrid demand bids take a monotonically decreasing form. Scope: Microgrid demand submissions to the DMO. The fixed nonresponsive-load portion of the demand bid cannot be altered. Scope: The fixed nonresponsive-load quantity in a microgrid demand bid. Condition: Under normal operation conditions.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.demand under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.demand","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e037"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"DMO aggregation of microgrid and other responsive-load demand bids for submission to the ISO. | Microgrid demand submissions to the DMO. | The fixed nonresponsive-load quantity in a microgrid demand bid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e037","v141-b-g02-E16"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-theta-df-mt","symbol":"d^{f}_{mt}","meaning":"Fixed nonresponsive load included in microgrid m's demand bid at hour t; the fixed part of the bid that must be fully supplied under normal operation and cannot be altered.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["m","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e031","v141-b-g01-e032","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R002-theta-Df-t","symbol":"D^{f}_{t}","meaning":"Total fixed nonresponsive load of all microgrids in the DMO service territory at hour t, obtained by summing the microgrid fixed loads in the aggregated bid.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e032","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DMO combines received demand bids and submits an aggregated demand bid to the ISO. Scope: DMO aggregation of microgrid and other responsive-load demand bids for submission to the ISO.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e037"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Microgrid demand bids take a monotonically decreasing form. Scope: Microgrid demand submissions to the DMO.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The fixed nonresponsive-load portion of the demand bid cannot be altered. Scope: The fixed nonresponsive-load quantity in a microgrid demand bid. Condition: Under normal operation conditions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The DMO obtains the total fixed nonresponsive load in its service territory at hour t by summing the fixed nonresponsive loads of the individual microgrid demand bids.","expression":"D^f_t = \\sum_m d^f_{mt} \\quad \\forall t.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-theta-df-mt","v141-c-R002-theta-Df-t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e032","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. Model Outline","anchor_text":"nd, The discussed DMO in this paper is a platform that enables ts, market activities for end-use cus","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Two major responsibilities of the DMO within this structure are: 1) To receive demand bids from the microgrids (and other responsive loads if any), combine them, and offer an aggregated bid to the ISO..."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. Model Outline","anchor_text":"li- vice territory, and subsequently determine microgrids shares ia, from the awarded power. Microgr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Microgrids would submit their bids to the DMO (in the form of monotonically decreasing demand bids) and later be notified by the DMO on the amount of awarded power (henceforth referred to as the assigned power)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e037","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"B. DMO / 1) Bid Aggregation","anchor_text":"ed is o- Fig. 2. Demand bid curve for microgrid m with a three-segment bid. by B. DMO nal es The DMO","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The DMO seeks two objectives: first, to combine individual bids received from microgrids in its territory to create an aggregated bid and accordingly send the aggregated bid to the ISO to participate in the energy market; second, to disaggregate the awarded quantity by the ISO to individual microgrids in accordance with their respective bids."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"B. DMO / 1) Bid Aggregation","anchor_text":"ed is o- Fig. 2. Demand bid curve for microgrid m with a three-segment bid. by B. DMO nal es The DMO","equation_id":"Eq. (11)","figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Fig. 2 depicts a typical demand bid curve submitted by a microgrid to the DMO at a specific hour t. The bid consists of fixed and variable parts. The fixed part shows the microgrid nonresponsive load which must be fully supplied under normal operation conditions and cannot be altered. The variable part, on the other hand, shows the microgrid flexibility in reducing its consumption from its total load. It consists of several segments. The reduction in consumption can be achieved either via load curtailment or local DER generation. The DMO combines the individual microgrid bids and obtains an aggregated bid to be sent to the ISO. The fixed loads are collectively added to obtain the total fixed load in the DMO service territory (11)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e031","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"B. DMO / 1) Bid Aggregation","anchor_text":"ed is o- Fig. 2. Demand bid curve for microgrid m with a three-segment bid. by B. DMO nal es The DMO","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Fig. 2 depicts a typical demand bid curve submitted by a microgrid to the DMO at a speciﬁc hour t. The bid consists of ﬁxed and variable parts. The ﬁxed part shows the microgrid nonresponsive load which must be fully supplied under normal operation conditions and cannot be altered. The variable part, on the other hand, shows the microgrid ﬂexibility in reducing its consumption from its total load. It consists of several segments. The reduction in consumption can be achieved either via load curtailment or local DER generation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e032","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"B. DMO / 1) Bid Aggregation","anchor_text":"or be altered. The variable part, on the other hand, shows the n- microgrid ﬂexibility in reducing i","equation_id":"Eq. (11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"D^f_t = \\sum_m d^f_{mt} \\quad \\forall t. \\quad (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"B. DMO / 1) Bid Aggregation","anchor_text":"or be altered. The variable part, on the other hand, shows the n- microgrid ﬂexibility in reducing i","equation_id":"Eq. (11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The fixed loads are collectively added to obtain the total fixed load in the DMO service territory (11).\nD_t^{f} = \\sum_m d_{mt}^{f} \\quad \\forall t. \\tag{11}"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This rule is bid submission/aggregation with a fixed-load accounting identity. The supplied bid-submission scope defines no design-selection or operational decision variable; the fixed bid components are treated as theta inputs. Segment award decisions DX belong to the DMO quantity-disaggregation rule, not this rule.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-matching","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","quote":"Two major responsibilities of the DMO within this structure are: 1) To receive demand bids from the microgrids (and other responsive loads if any), combine them, and offer an aggregated bid to the ISO"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e037","quote":"The DMO seeks two objectives: first, to combine individual bids received from microgrids in its territory to create an aggregated bid and accordingly send the aggregated bid to the ISO to participate in the energy market;"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","quote":"Microgrids would submit their bids to the DMO (in the form of monotonically decreasing demand bids)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E16","quote":"The bid consists of fixed and variable parts. The fixed part shows the microgrid nonresponsive load which must be fully supplied under normal operation conditions and cannot be altered."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"42e26a7b0a22c4a40a6ccf09d744ffd524b2d4d3b0e2b1b04300b29517e4bee8","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Formalized only Eq. (11), the fixed-load aggregation identity supported by the bid-aggregation text. The existing procedural clauses (bid receipt, aggregation, submission to the ISO, monotonically decreasing bid form, and unalterable fixed nonresponsive load) are preserved without expressions because the supplied source states them qualitatively and does not provide an explicit segment-ordering inequality or a full aggregate-bid equation. The declared theta objects are fixed bid inputs or aggregate fixed-load quantities, not DMO optimization decisions. B evidence is unreviewed; no independent source review is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-theta-df-mt","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"d^{f}_{mt} is the fixed nonresponsive portion of a microgrid's submitted demand bid, so it belongs to bidding.demand. It is an input fixed quantity for bid aggregation, not a DMO operational decision."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-theta-Df-t","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"D^{f}_{t} is the DMO-level aggregate fixed-load component of the bid, linking the DMO's coordination role to demand bidding through the existing local_operator-to-demand edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Equation (11) formalizes the fixed-load aggregation part of the DMO's bid-combination role under the existing local_operator-to-demand edge. It does not assert a full variable-bid aggregation formula that the supplied source does not state explicitly."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
